# GitHub CI

`.github/workflows/ci.yml` runs on **push to `main`/`develop`** and **pull_request into those**. A feature-branch push is a no-op until a PR exists.

## Watch CI on the public site

Do **not** block on `gh auth login` or GitHub MCP `mcp_auth` (that prompt has hung this repo). Git push already works over HTTPS.

Monitor with unauthenticated HTTP:

- Actions: https://github.com/RickZee/ai-team/actions
- Branch runs: https://github.com/RickZee/ai-team/actions?query=branch%3Afeature%2Fphase-harness-alignment
- API: `https://api.github.com/repos/RickZee/ai-team/actions/runs?branch=<branch>`
- Releases: https://github.com/RickZee/ai-team/releases
- Compare / open PR: https://github.com/RickZee/ai-team/compare/main...<branch>

`gh run view` is optional when `gh` is already authenticated.

## After a push that should run CI

1. Confirm a PR into `main` or `develop` exists (or open one via the compare URL / git credentials).
2. Poll the public Actions API or page until jobs complete.
3. If red, follow `.cursor/skills/fix-ci/SKILL.md` from the failed job name.
